  "final_scientific_verdict": {
    "verdict": "NO MATERIAL IMPROVEMENT",
    "rationale": "While augmenting camera-space features with explicit orientation descriptors (Variant B, 296d) provided modest improvements over a newly retrained 280d baseline (+1.36% on signer_04_val, +2.22% on pure cross-signer transfer, and protected critical letters H, R, L, Y), no candidate variant outperformed the frozen production Model C, which already achieves 100.00% on signer_04_val and exhibits substantially superior robustness under controlled in-plane tilt (81.3%-92.5% vs 56.2%-79.5% for retrained variants). Furthermore, appending canonical pose coordinates (Variants C and D) caused regressions in pure cross-signer transfer (38.74% and 35.04% vs 40.16%). Therefore, there is no material justification to alter the frozen 280-dimensional feature schema or retrain production Model C."
  },
